[ceiling] Required fore meter carrier neck: this flat face is the fore collar's dogleg between its seat and the corbelled wall lane (`_back_top_meter`), passing fore of the fixed gas-drop column. A 45-degree roofward corbel over it either rises into the standing CO2 tube (X74.4-81.4, Y364.8-371.9) on its way to the wall or closes the collar tie's path up through its slot (X66-68). Tree(auto)/Default support stands under it through the open interior (slice 257a5648, interfaces 33 and 34) and leaves before the meter goes in. Physical cleanup remains unqualified.
alternatives: Moving the neck changes the collar's fixed bearing; a corbel short of the tube and the tie leaves the same face flat.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
click: x=65.525 y=367.707 z=297.076

[ceiling] Required forward lever-nut well top: the middle WAGO 221-413's well (`above_core_wiring`, wago-n) stands 14.5 mm forward of the stack's tower, and this is its top there. The upper lever nut's front half and its PE leads stand 8 mm over it, so no corbel fits. Tree(auto)/Default support stands under it through the open interior (slice 257a5648, interface 12) and leaves before the nuts are fitted. Physical cleanup remains unqualified.
alternatives: Setting the well back into the tower moves the lever nut's station; a corbel over it enters the upper nut and its leads.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
click: x=-34.000 y=447.250 z=323.550

[ceiling] Required lever-nut well floors: each WAGO 221-413 rests on its well's 19.1 x 9.5 mm floor, which back-top's ceiling-down print lays as a bridge between the well's 3 mm side walls; slice 257a5648 places no support under any of the three.
alternatives: A floor of end tabs, as the flank wells have (`wago_roof_tab`), leaves two 2 mm ledges and opens the nut's underside.
