[ceiling] Required upper M5 passage-relief floors: these level ends stop the 5.2 mm passage slots where the clearance bore crosses the sloped middle-knuckle face. They remove the knife edge at that crossing. Back-top prints roof-down; retain Tree(auto)/Default and remove support through the exposed seam and bore before fitting the screw. Physical cleanup remains unqualified.
alternatives: Filling the relief restores the bore-to-face knife edge. A sloped end meets the knuckle face in an arris; extending the slot through the block removes the retained bearing section.
