[ceiling] Required full-section ends of the upper middle knuckle: these flats stop its rising face one nominal wall short of the free edge, preserving a square end and the running clearance to front-top's head block. Back-top prints roof-down. Tree(auto)/Default support leaves through the exposed seam before assembly; actual cleanup remains unqualified.
alternatives: Running the slope to the free edge makes a tapered tip. Filling upward enters the head block's running envelope. Removing the end reduces the middle knuckle's retained section.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
