[sliver] Required cable-retaining undercuts: these are the complete flat working undersides of the DC-1 pair, bare J5 4P ribbon and V-K positive-lead catches, respectively 0.75 x 16, 0.75 x 16 and 0.60 x 8 mm. The three hooks keep 3 mm arm stock; the measured strip width is the catch projection into the entry, setting the 2.75, 1.45 and 1.60 mm mouths in their 3.50, 2.20 and 2.20 mm deep seats (`cadlib/route_snap.py:cable_hook`). The 16 mm J5 section has Derek's fit/retention acceptance in future/snap-fit-tests/2026-10-26-mark2-combined/physical-result.json. The DC-1 and V-K section fits and the complete enclosure print remain unqualified.
alternatives: A 3 mm projection closes either 2.20 mm seat's mouth and leaves only 0.50 mm at the DC-1 entry. Enlarging the whole hook to retain its mouth enlarges the matched cable seat and requires another fit/clearance review. Filling beneath the flat enters the cable seat; removing the projection opens retention, and sloping the working underside makes withdrawal spread the hook along a release ramp.
