[ledge] Required cable catch bearings: these are the same complete flat retention undersides of the V-K, DC-1 and J5 hooks, 0.60 x 8, 0.75 x 16 and 0.75 x 16 mm, in the ceiling-down production pose. Their square undercuts hold the cable behind its narrower entry; the surrounding arm stock is 3 mm. J5's 16 mm section has the specific physical fit/retention acceptance in future/snap-fit-tests/2026-10-26-mark2-combined/physical-result.json; that result does not qualify the other two seats or the full enclosure's support cleanup.
alternatives: A sloped bearing is a withdrawal ramp; filling under it closes the cable seat. A 3 mm bearing projection closes the two 2.20 mm seats' mouths and restricts the 3.50 mm seat to a 0.50 mm entry. Enlarging the complete seat changes the fitted cable envelope. Support placement for the complete enclosure belongs to its own native print preparation.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
