[thin] Accepted C2 spring section: these two readings are the free 2.40 mm radial wings of the Reservoir A fill clip, with the selected 6.35 mm bore, 125.421 degree wrap per wing and 8 mm axial span. Derek selected this C2 bore and wing section for present use in future/snap-fit-tests/2026-10-26-mark2-combined/physical-result.json. The answer covers the working spring arms; it does not qualify fatigue, numerical holding force or the complete enclosure print.
alternatives: Thickening the free arms to 3 mm changes the accepted spring section, its outer envelope and insertion response. Filling between the arms closes insertion; reducing their wrap changes the accepted retention geometry. A separate cap changes the requested integral interface.
