[ceiling] Required common gas-carrier boundary: the two fixed-barrel seats share one 8 mm slab on Z293/301. The gas bodies, adjustment parts and collets occupy the space above that footprint. Tree(auto)/Default remains under the carrier; the source-bound Mark2 slice and its local support-path reading are in enclosure/enclosure/plain-mount-review. Physical support release remains unqualified.
alternatives: Continuing the complete footprint to the roof enters the installed gas bodies. Retreating to a narrower roof column requires additional carrier transitions and long strap passages; a corbel requires further cuts around the gas bodies. The common flat slab preserves the selected bearings and one plain stock boundary.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
click: x=88.350 y=407.364 z=301.000

[ceiling] Required straight meter-strap passage profiles: both 3 mm high openings retain the 3 mm web over the collar seats. Their closed portions, X52.5 to X63, contain no support roads in the native Mark2 slice. The fore opening joins the west-open ASSE approach, where automatic tree support remains accessible before installing hardware; this is not a claim of physically easy release.
alternatives: A gable consumes the lower web unless the passage moves upward; that adds profile breaks and requires redrawing the fore ASSE overlap. Filling either opening closes the retaining-strap path. The straight openings retain the complete nominal strip section and the broad column faces.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
